Snuffel data and shared code - licences

Data
- Places and data derived from them (dist/, the place data the pipeline builds):
  © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0,
  https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright and https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/.
  When you reuse them: credit "© OpenStreetMap contributors" and keep derived databases
  under the ODbL.
- Basemap: Protomaps (BSD 3-Clause / ODbL). Country outlines: Natural Earth (public domain).

Everything else
- Code (lib/, tools/, tests/), language packs (i18n/), the lost-dog guide and its lists
  (lost/) and the documentation: Copyright (c) 2026 De Wit Automatisering B.V.
  (KvK 82248508, the Netherlands). All rights reserved, unless a file says otherwise.
- This repository is public so that anyone can see how Snuffel's data and rules are made.
  That doesn't grant a licence: reading is fine; copying, modifying or redistributing the
  code or texts requires permission (support@snuffel.app), except as the law allows.
- Third-party components keep their own licences.
